# 15. Two important limits

First, **dimensionful numbers cannot be predicted without an endogenous scale**. A theory can derive mass ratios and dimensionless combinations, but quoting a mass in MeV presupposes a unit-bearing record. The clean targets are therefore

[
\alpha_i,\quad
\frac{m_i}{m_j},\quad
\frac{m_i}{m_P},\quad
\Lambda\ell_P^2,
]

with one common scale produced by dimensional transmutation, a spectral gap, or a gravitational state.

Second, I would resist adding parameter-specific axioms such as:

* “choose the larger Koide root”;
* “the matching scale is (10^{13},\mathrm{GeV})”;
* “the cosmological trigger is Step 16”;
* “maximize a quantity until the observed angle appears.”

Those encode outcomes. The stronger additions above instead specify **how numbers may lawfully become determinate**.

# Bottom line

The most important new axiom is:

[
\boxed{\text{No publicly inequivalent primitive continuum without an internal provenance certificate.}}
]

From that, the most promising near-term extensions are:

[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{append-only representation}
&&\Rightarrow q_\nu=0,\ \text{charge lattice},\
&\text{complete-probe effectivity}
&&\Rightarrow G_{\mathrm{SM}}/\mathbb Z_6,\
&\text{no unpaid multiplicity}
&&\Rightarrow N_H=1,\
&\text{orientation witness}
&&\Rightarrow N_{\mathrm{gen}}=3,\
&\text{depth-two Cauchy closure}
&&\Rightarrow S_{\mathrm{EH}}+\text{minimal field dynamics},\
&\text{public central indifference}
&&\Rightarrow Q_3=2/3,\
&\text{no unrecorded topological phase}
&&\Rightarrow \bar\theta=0.
\end{aligned}
}
]

The first serious continuous-constant campaign should then combine the canonical public quadratic form with an isolated RG boundary-value problem. That is a substantially more credible target than trying immediately to derive the entire flavor spectrum: it could, in one coherent calculation, address the weak matching scale, low-energy gauge couplings, Higgs quartic, and top Yukawa while producing an unambiguous residual count of whatever parameters remain free.

